<article class="env-lemma" id="019Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/019Z">Lemma <span data-tag="019Z">14.28.5</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of a category $\mathcal{C}$ with pushouts. Assume there is a morphism $s : Y \to X$ with $s \circ f = \text{id}_ X$. Consider the cosimplicial object $U$ constructed in Example <a href="/tag/016N" data-tag="016N">14.5.5</a> starting with $f$. The morphism $U \to U$ which in each degree is the self map of $Y \amalg _ X \ldots \amalg _ X Y$ given by $f \circ s$ on each factor is homotopic to the identity on $U$. In particular, $U$ is homotopy equivalent to the constant cosimplicial object $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This lemma is dual to Lemma <a href="/tag/019P" data-tag="019P">14.26.9</a>. Hence this lemma follows on applying Lemma <a href="/tag/019X" data-tag="019X">14.28.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>